    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d435">

                <pb facs="0638" n="538" xml:id="pg538"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">868.51 War Credits/654: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Greece</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">MacVeagh</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Athens</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1934-03-09T12:00:00+02:00">March 9,
                        1934—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received March 9—11:35 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>26. Your 16, March 7, 8 p.m. The Foreign Minister told me last night that the
                    Greek Government had not yet issued the instructions referred to but had on
                    March 7 addressed a letter to the International Financial Commission requesting
                    permission to do so at once exempting payments to such creditors as still insist
                    on payments on gold basis. This morning he requested me to inform you that the
                    United States 1929 loan will be given equal treatment under the same
                    reservations as last year.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">MacVeagh</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
